<section class="card" aria-labelledby="questions-heading">
  <h2 class="card__title" id="questions-heading">Questions</h2>
  <div class="content">
    <h3>Is there a free trial?</h3>
    <p>
      Yes, 14 days. You aren&rsquo;t charged until the trial ends, and you can cancel before then and pay nothing. After that, you can still ask for a refund within 14 days of any payment. See our <a href="/refunds/">Refund Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>How do I cancel?</h3>
    <p>
      Use the link in your Paddle email, or go to <a href="https://www.paddle.net" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">paddle.net</a> and look up your order. If you cancel during the trial, you won&rsquo;t be charged. If you cancel later, you can keep using the app until the end of the month you&rsquo;ve paid for, and you won&rsquo;t be charged again.
    </p>

    <h3>Who am I buying from?</h3>
    <p>
      Our order process is conducted by our online reseller Paddle.com. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our orders. Paddle takes the payment, charges the right tax for your country (including GST in Australia), and sends your receipts. The software comes from Daniel Hampton, trading as Practical Supply Chain Planning (ABN 56 757 743 802), Queensland, Australia.
    </p>

    <h3>Will I get a tax invoice?</h3>
    <p>
      Yes, from Paddle. Paddle emails a receipt for every payment, and you can download invoices from the link in that email or at <a href="https://www.paddle.net" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">paddle.net</a>. As the seller, Paddle charges and pays the GST on Australian orders.
    </p>

    <h3>What happens if a payment fails?</h3>
    <p>
      Paddle will retry the payment and email you. The app keeps working for 7 days from the first failed payment and shows a &ldquo;payment required&rdquo; message. If the payment still hasn&rsquo;t gone through after those 7 days, the app stops until it is paid. If Paddle can&rsquo;t collect the payment after its retries, the subscription is cancelled.
    </p>

    <h3>Can I use it on more than one PC?</h3>
    <p>
      One licence works on one PC at a time. If you get a new PC, email us and we&rsquo;ll move your licence across. If you need more PCs, buy a second subscription.
    </p>

    <h3>Do I need an internet connection?</h3>
    <p>
      Only now and then. The app needs the internet to activate, then it checks your licence about once a week. It keeps working for up to 14 days without a connection.
    </p>

    <h3>Will Windows warn me when I install it?</h3>
    <p>
      Windows SmartScreen may show &ldquo;Windows protected your PC&rdquo; and &ldquo;Unknown publisher&rdquo;, because Practical Stock Planner isn&rsquo;t code-signed yet. To continue, click &ldquo;More info&rdquo;, then &ldquo;Run anyway&rdquo;. The download comes only from practicalsupplychainplanning.com. Code signing is planned.
    </p>

